WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.339 line:82%
Chapter 8. Activities and games. They are for practice, and they never count as Test 1 or Test 2.

00:00:08.764 --> 00:00:18.007 line:82%
Open "Activities and games". There are four doors: Speak and share, Listen and read, Games with phones, and Games without phones.

00:00:18.471 --> 00:00:25.787 line:82%
Speak and share. A live poll: write a question and 2 to 6 choices, then press "Open on the screen".

00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:35.088 line:82%
Students tap their name and vote. The bars grow live on the screen.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:46.107 line:82%
A word cloud works the same way. Each student sends up to 3 words. You check every word first, and the screen never shows names.

00:01:04.894 --> 00:01:13.330 line:82%
This door also has the idea wall, discussion cards, speed chat, and Time to speak. Chapter 12 shows Time to speak.

00:01:13.788 --> 00:01:25.276 line:82%
Listen and read: a listening for every lesson of your book, a video quiz, a song gap-fill, a levelled reading, and a dictation. Chapter 17 shows the listening.

00:01:25.736 --> 00:01:34.796 line:82%
For example, the song gap-fill. Paste the words of the song, and press "Choose words for me". The app hides one useful word in each line.

00:01:35.248 --> 00:01:38.796 line:82%
Games with phones. Choose a game and a lesson.

00:01:39.258 --> 00:01:46.277 line:82%
The team quiz. Choose the number of teams, and how to make them: at random, mixed levels, or by seats.

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:52.776 line:82%
Press "Open the waiting room". Students join as usual, and each phone shows the team.

00:02:01.984 --> 00:02:11.898 line:82%
The first two times a class plays a game, Ollie the owl explains how to play, on the projector and on the phones. Then students try a practice turn.

00:02:12.358 --> 00:02:21.624 line:82%
Press "Close" when everyone understands. Then everyone answers on their own phone. A team gets more points when more of its members are right.

00:02:25.971 --> 00:02:36.365 line:82%
The coin race. Each student answers non-stop on their phone. Right answers earn coins, and coins buy power-ups: double, shield, freeze and steal.

00:03:05.978 --> 00:03:12.322 line:82%
The boss battle. The whole class plays together against a monster. Every right answer hits it.

00:03:39.032 --> 00:03:52.799 line:82%
There are many more: escape room, survival, treasure chests, climb race, impostor, draw and guess, fake answer, team race, two truths and a lie, and the detective mystery. Each one starts the same way.

00:03:53.256 --> 00:04:04.500 line:82%
Impostor is like Among Us. The app secretly makes some students impostors. The crew answers questions to fix the ship. Then the class talks in English, and votes.

00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:25.446 line:82%
Games without phones. The board game: teams take turns to choose a square. Behind each square is a question worth 10, 20 or 30 points, or a surprise.

00:04:26.135 --> 00:04:30.748 line:82%
The team answers aloud. Press "Show answer", then give the points.

00:04:31.218 --> 00:04:39.827 line:82%
Hot seat: one student sits with their back to the screen, and the team describes the word in the picture. Press "Got it" or "Pass".

00:04:47.804 --> 00:04:56.706 line:82%
"Spin the wheel" picks a student who is here today, a question from a lesson, or anything from your own list. Click the wheel to spin it.

00:04:57.827 --> 00:05:06.926 line:82%
Flashcards show word cards big on the board. On the phones, students can play a match race, or study the cards alone. Have fun!
